{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01CJhRc5G32Q8B1ScaXSbQeY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both gates green — `green-verify` (290 default-suite tests, immutability OK) and `verify-all` with the process suite (38 files, 325 tests). All Definition-of-Done items check out: TC-5.1–5.5 green, all five CLI commands proven through the spawned binary, the profile-violation and missing-thread legs pass, Story 4's CLI-intake-advances-boundary debt and Story 3's TC-3.3 CLI receipt leg are closed, the format fixture is committed with its provenance note, and every spawned CLI call runs with `LHC_PROVIDER` stripped.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-verification\",\n  \"planSummary\": \"Format fixture first: trimmed a real PI session file (PI 0.79.1, session version 3) into test/fixtures/pi-session-structure.jsonl with a provenance note, and a conformance helper that derives required shapes from the fixture at runtime. Then materialize over pull output: refactored the pull assembly in thread-view/index.ts into one shared assembleView() that both pull and materialize consume (parity by construction — internal/materialize.ts never sees a DB handle), with entry ids/timestamps derived from message ids, event recorded_at, and view created-at (never write-time clocks; tail rows now carry recorded_at via an event join, and thread_metadata feeds the header — the sanctioned fix-pull's-output path). Added the unknown_format caller error. Then cli/view.ts with the full pinned grammar (five commands, band-override flags merged field-wise before validation, --no-sweep, --json, --out, --format), routed ahead of the shared flag parser so its flags don't widen other commands. Finally the process suite: TC-5.4, parity legs for all five commands on twin fixture threads, the profile-violation and missing-thread nonzero legs, TC-3.3's CLI receipt-shape leg via the shared schema, and the CLI-intake-advances-boundary leg (spawned intake over default max → spawned pull shows abridged flips, spawned status zone ≤ target). Two hash-locked tests amended under the established sanctioned-amendment pattern (Story 2/3 precedent) with the manifest re-recorded.\",\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts\", \"reason\": \"new unknown_format caller-error code for materialize's format check (story Scope: unknown format names accepted values)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/snapshot.ts\", \"reason\": \"tail rows gain recordedAt (event join) and readThreadMetadata() — materialize's generated fields derive from record/view metadata, never write-time clocks (AC-5.2)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/materialize.ts\", \"reason\": \"new PI session JSONL writer: pure mapping from pull entries (header, parentId chain, text-block encoding) plus the file write; never sees a DB handle (must-not-own)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"pull assembly extracted into shared assembleView(); materialize implemented over the same entry array (AC-5.3 parity structural), touch-suppressed, format-validated; stub and notImplemented helper removed\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/cli/view.ts\", \"reason\": \"new lhc view pull|status|compact|sweep|materialize adapter per the pinned grammar; calls the domain surface directly so no provider exists on the path\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"routes the view group to its own parser (keeps view flags out of the shared flag set); help text gains the five commands\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/vitest.config.ts\", \"reason\": \"cli-process-view.test.ts added to the process-suite-only exclude list\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/pi-session-structure.jsonl\", \"reason\": \"structure-trimmed REAL PI session file (anti-shim: from PI output, not the design's description)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/pi-session-structure.provenance.md\", \"reason\": \"provenance note: source session, PI coding agent 0.79.1 / session format v3, trim applied (DoD item)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/pi-session-format.ts\", \"reason\": \"conformance checker deriving header/entry/block shapes from the fixture at runtime (TC-5.3/TC-5.5), shared by both suites\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"re-export the conformance helpers\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-render-targets.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"TC-5.1, TC-5.2 (+unknown-format leg), TC-5.3, TC-5.5 through the real SDK surface\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-view.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"TC-5.4 plus all deferred process legs: five-command parity, profile-violation, missing-thread, TC-3.3 CLI receipt shape, CLI-intake-advances-boundary; every spawn strips LHC_PROVIDER\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"sanctioned amendment: retired the materialize not-implemented skeleton test (the operation is real; view-render-targets owns it) — same pattern Stories 2/3 used\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/view-sweep.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"sanctioned amendment: zero-provider five-op test now expects materialize ok:true (still zero provider calls)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"re-recorded hashes for the two amended files; locked the two new test files\" }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": {\n    \"added\": [\n      \"view-render-targets: TC-5.1 bands in gradient order with labels, tail in record order, byte-identical repeated pulls\",\n      \"view-render-targets: TC-5.2 materialize/pull item-for-item parity, view-metadata-derived ids/timestamps, byte-identical repeat, full thread-state hash unchanged\",\n      \"view-render-targets: unknown format rejected naming pi-session, nothing written\",\n      \"view-render-targets: TC-5.3 never-compacted tail-only file, header from thread created-at, fixture-conformant\",\n      \"view-render-targets: TC-5.5 conformance against the real-PI structure fixture incl. explicit parentId chain\",\n      \"cli-process-view: spawned sweep receipt passes shared schema and equals SDK twin (TC-3.3 CLI leg)\",\n      \"cli-process-view: spawned compact with band flags equals SDK twin receipt, embedded sweep included\",\n      \"cli-process-view: profile violation exits nonzero naming the sum constraint\",\n      \"cli-process-view: spawned pull/status JSON equal SDK reads of the same thread (TC-5.4)\",\n      \"cli-process-view: spawned materialize prints path; file conforms and is byte-identical to the SDK's\",\n      \"cli-process-view: unknown --format exits nonzero naming accepted values\",\n      \"cli-process-view: missing thread exits nonzero with structured thread_not_found on all five commands\",\n      \"cli-process-view: spawned CLI intake over max advances the boundary — pull shows flips, status zone ≤ target (Story 4 debt)\"\n    ],\n    \"modified\": [\n      \"view-pull.test.ts (sanctioned amendment: materialize stub test removed)\",\n      \"view-sweep.test.ts (sanctioned amendment: materialize expectation flipped to ok:true in the zero-provider five-op test)\"\n    ],\n    \"removed\": [\n      \"view-pull: 'materialize returns ok:false not-implemented, never throws' (operation is real now)\"\n    ],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 325,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 12\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm run green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm run verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [\n      \"TC-5.3 initially expected 5 file entries; turn_end projects no message so the never-compacted thread renders 4 — assertion corrected with a comment explaining why\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"Header id format (threadId:createdAt) and header cwd (thread file's directory) are deterministic choices the tech design does not pin beyond 'derives from thread id + view createdAt' and the cwd field's existence — both satisfy byte-identical repeats; flag if the PI extension expects a UUID-shaped id or a real cwd\",\n      \"--json is accepted per the pinned grammar but is a no-op: output is always JSON per the Epic 01/02 CLI convention (documented in --help)\",\n      \"user-role content is encoded as a text-block array (PI accepts both string and block array for user; assistant requires the array) — one uniform encoding keeps the writer simple\",\n      \"Two Red-locked test files were amended and the manifest re-recorded, following the explicit sanctioned-amendment precedent from Stories 2 and 3\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"specDeviations\": [],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Story verification: review the sanctioned amendments to view-pull/view-sweep and the header id/cwd derivation choices, then run the epic-level acceptance pass — this story closes the epic's last open debts (process suite now 'ran', Story 3 and Story 4 deferred legs green).\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":273,"cache_read_input_tokens":202054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":273},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d96b6140-abf0-4148-ae10-52f37fa752e0","uuid":"9c028840-f5e1-468b-be1b-623bf856a1e7","request_id":"req_011CbwvKWzfFFvqFNkSqNsJ2"}
